              "body": "EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT PHYSICIAN NOTE\nArrival 12/24/2023 14:05. Sent in by her PCP.\n\nCC: joint pain and fever x3 days.\n\nHPI: 26 y/o F with prior recurrent condylomata and remote molluscum, here with three days of fevers and progressively worse joint pain. Right knee and left wrist painful and swollen, as are several fingers; trouble gripping things and walking. Since yesterday a painful rash of red bumps and tiny blisters on both forearms and ankles. A week of on-and-off lower abdominal discomfort with vaginal spotting, plus a yellowish discharge, no itching, no odor. LMP 2 weeks ago. Sexually active with multiple partners, barrier protection inconsistent. Denies IV drug use.\n\nPMH: condylomata acuminata, molluscum contagiosum. PSH none. Meds none. NKDA. FH: mother hypothyroidism, father HTN, sibling healthy. SH: never smoker, social alcohol.\n\nExam: T 38.9, HR 112, BP 118/72, RR 18, SpO2 98% RA. Febrile, uncomfortable-appearing. Left wrist and right knee swollen with reduced range of motion. Tender along the flexor tendon sheaths of the left hand. Scattered pustules on erythematous bases over the distal arms and legs. Heart tachycardic, regular; lungs clear; abdomen soft. Speculum: cervix friable with mucopurulent discharge. No cervical motion tenderness. No adnexal tenderness.\n\nED course: CBC, CMP, CRP, ESR, urine hCG, blood cultures x2. Cervical swab for GC/CT NAAT. Right knee arthrocentesis under sterile technique, fluid sent for cell count, crystals, Gram stain and culture. HIV and RPR sent. Ceftriaxone 1 g IV given. Repeat T 38.4, HR 104.\n\nWBC 13.4 (82% PMN). CRP 96. ESR 48. CMP unremarkable. hCG negative. Synovial fluid inflammatory; Gram stain without organisms.\n\nAssessment: suspected disseminated gonococcal infection with arthritis, tenosynovitis and dermatitis, plus cervicitis.\nDisposition: admitted to medicine for IV ceftriaxone.\n\nAddendum 12/25: cervical NAAT positive for N. gonorrhoeae, negative for C. trachomatis. Diagnosis confirmed."
            }
          ]
