              "date": "2024-01-02T10:15",
              "body": "DISCHARGE SUMMARY\nAdmitted 12/24/2023. Discharged 12/30/2023.\nAdmitting/discharge diagnosis: disseminated gonococcal infection (arthritis-dermatitis), with gonococcal cervicitis.\n\nHospital course: 26 year old woman admitted from the ED with fever, polyarthritis of the right knee and left wrist, left hand flexor tenosynovitis and pustular skin lesions of the distal extremities. Cervical NAAT returned positive for gonorrhea, negative for chlamydia. Blood cultures x2 no growth at 5 days. Right knee synovial fluid: WBC 42,000, 88% neutrophils, no crystals, Gram stain negative, culture no growth. HIV and RPR nonreactive.\n\nTreated with ceftriaxone 1 g IV every 24 hours, 7 doses, completed before discharge. Fevers resolved by hospital day 2. Joint swelling and skin lesions improved steadily. Day 4 labs: WBC 9.1, CRP 31 (from 96).\n\nPartner notification and testing discussed; she has the information to share with recent partners. Abstain from sex until partners are treated and her symptoms are gone. Repeat GC/CT testing in about 3 months.\n\nDischarge medications: none.\nAllergies: NKDA.\nCondition at discharge: afebrile, ambulating, improved.\nFollow-up: PCP within one week."
